1
00:01:54,959 --> 00:01:56,280
Ding Ning found me!

2
00:01:56,319 --> 00:01:57,719
Your turn to hide, your turn to hide!

3
00:01:57,719 --> 00:01:59,040
It's your turn to catch us!

4
00:01:59,519 --> 00:02:01,120
Just hide in this closet.

5
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:09,680
Why were you hiding in there?

6
00:02:09,680 --> 00:02:10,479
Why?

7
00:02:13,439 --> 00:02:15,120
I wanted to play hide-and-seek with you.

8
00:02:17,199 --> 00:02:17,879
Then when I called you,

9
00:02:17,879 --> 00:02:19,360
why didn't you say anything?

10
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:20,759
You scared me to death!

11
00:02:23,479 --> 00:02:24,639
Don't be scared, Ding Ning.

12
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:27,439
Awu will never scare you again.

13
00:02:56,639 --> 00:02:57,240
Grandpa.

14
00:02:58,360 --> 00:02:59,439
Grandpa.

15
00:03:02,800 --> 00:03:03,960
You're still awake?

16
00:03:08,879 --> 00:03:10,240
Where did you guys go last night?

17
00:03:11,039 --> 00:03:12,639
You all love pulling disappearing acts.

18
00:03:13,919 --> 00:03:15,120
We just went to buy vinegar.

19
00:03:15,159 --> 00:03:16,560
It took you all night to buy vinegar?

20
00:03:16,879 --> 00:03:17,840
And you didn't answer your phones.

21
00:03:20,439 --> 00:03:22,919
Because hardly any places are open for the New Year.

22
00:03:23,560 --> 00:03:25,719
So Zhao Yijie said we should drive around looking.

23
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:27,919
Then the car broke down halfway.

24
00:03:28,120 --> 00:03:29,879
We called for a tow truck.

25
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:32,680
They said no one works until New Year's Day.

26
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:33,520
Tell me the truth.

27
00:03:33,520 --> 00:03:34,479
Did something happen?

28
00:03:36,479 --> 00:03:38,159
So we waited until just now...

29
00:03:39,039 --> 00:03:40,240
and... and just got back.

30
00:03:40,240 --> 00:03:42,280
I didn't sleep all night.

31
00:03:42,960 --> 00:03:44,319
I smell terrible right now.

32
00:03:44,319 --> 00:03:45,680
I'll go take a shower first.

33
00:03:47,680 --> 00:03:49,439
Then I'll make breakfast for you when I get out.

34
00:03:49,439 --> 00:03:50,439
What do you want to eat?

35
00:03:52,560 --> 00:03:53,400
I'm not eating.

36
00:03:55,039 --> 00:03:56,199
I have something to do in a bit.

37
00:03:56,800 --> 00:03:57,639
Okay, okay.

38
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:04,280
Ding Ning, come back early.

39
00:04:04,639 --> 00:04:06,599
It's New Year's Day, we should be together.

40
00:04:08,599 --> 00:04:09,400
Got it.

41
00:04:09,840 --> 00:04:11,479
I'll come back and spend time with you once I'm done, okay?

42
00:04:32,519 --> 00:04:33,199
Happy New Year.

43
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:34,839
Happy New Year.

44
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:36,959
I came back to drop off some New Year gifts

45
00:04:36,959 --> 00:04:38,120
and pick up a few things.

46
00:04:39,839 --> 00:04:40,399
Here.

47
00:04:54,120 --> 00:04:55,360
My memory's not too bad, right?

48
00:04:55,839 --> 00:04:56,839
It's been so many years,

49
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,040
but I still remember what you taught me.

50
00:04:59,079 --> 00:05:00,360
I haven't played in years.

51
00:05:05,199 --> 00:05:06,279
When you were little,

52
00:05:06,279 --> 00:05:07,720
you often wouldn't speak for a whole day.

53
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:10,600
Then at night, you'd scream in your sleep.

54
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:12,199
And they were heart-wrenching.

55
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:14,279
Back then, they didn't really talk about depression.

56
00:05:14,800 --> 00:05:16,680
The doctor said something must have terrified you.

57
00:05:16,720 --> 00:05:17,680
Like you had hysteria.

58
00:05:18,879 --> 00:05:20,399
It wasn't that I didn't want to speak.

59
00:05:20,800 --> 00:05:21,879
You know how it was.

60
00:05:22,639 --> 00:05:23,839
Whenever I said anything back then,

61
00:05:23,839 --> 00:05:25,319
Mom's slap was waiting for me.

62
00:05:26,279 --> 00:05:27,040
Do you remember

63
00:05:27,040 --> 00:05:28,360
back when I was a freshman in college?

64
00:05:28,360 --> 00:05:30,240
Once, I couldn't help but bring up that incident.

65
00:05:30,879 --> 00:05:32,040
And Mom slapped me all the same.

66
00:05:32,079 --> 00:05:33,480
Of course I remember that time.

67
00:05:33,720 --> 00:05:34,839
It really scared me, too.

68
00:05:36,199 --> 00:05:38,560
Mom was definitely too strict with you.

69
00:05:45,160 --> 00:05:46,639
Good thing you learned to play the piano.

70
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:48,439
You always seemed better when you played.

71
00:05:51,079 --> 00:05:53,040
Because you could play the things you couldn't say.

72
00:05:56,319 --> 00:05:57,600
I still remember when we were little,

73
00:05:58,000 --> 00:05:59,120
I'd secretly watch you play the piano.

74
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:00,839
Even back then, I knew

75
00:06:01,120 --> 00:06:02,000
you were different from us.

76
00:06:02,800 --> 00:06:05,240
You were playing to heal your own wounds.

77
00:06:06,279 --> 00:06:07,160
And later on,

78
00:06:07,439 --> 00:06:08,519
you didn't even need the piano anymore.

79
00:06:09,279 --> 00:06:11,000
Because you made yourself strong enough.

80
00:06:11,639 --> 00:06:13,079
So strong that nothing could bring you down.

81
00:06:16,959 --> 00:06:18,639
Honestly, I sometimes envy you.

82
00:06:21,839 --> 00:06:24,279
I used to often wish I could be like you,

83
00:06:24,839 --> 00:06:26,600
able to get along with Mom and Dad so naturally.

84
00:06:27,240 --> 00:06:27,839
Because compared to me,

85
00:06:27,839 --> 00:06:29,360
the three of you felt more like a family.

86
00:06:29,720 --> 00:06:30,439
Try one.

87
00:06:36,199 --> 00:06:36,959
I'm not being jealous.

88
00:06:36,959 --> 00:06:38,040
I really mean it.

89
00:06:40,399 --> 00:06:41,439
How could you think that?

90
00:06:42,240 --> 00:06:43,360
Actually, Mom and Dad always treated you...

91
00:06:45,079 --> 00:06:45,879
What's wrong?

92
00:06:51,959 --> 00:06:53,000
The mold spots are gone.

93
00:06:55,199 --> 00:06:55,959
Mold spots?

94
00:06:56,240 --> 00:06:57,079
Where are the mold spots?

95
00:06:58,040 --> 00:06:59,319
There were never any mold spots there.

96
00:07:07,879 --> 00:07:08,680
Awu.

97
00:07:09,399 --> 00:07:10,959
What do you want for dinner?

98
00:07:10,959 --> 00:07:12,279
Grandpa will cook it for you, okay?

99
00:07:13,319 --> 00:07:14,120
I don't want to eat.

100
00:07:14,120 --> 00:07:15,600
I want to play with Xiao Lu.

101
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:17,600
Xiao Lu? What Xiao Lu?

102
00:07:17,839 --> 00:07:18,720
Lu Zhiyong.

103
00:07:18,959 --> 00:07:21,040
He often takes me to play at other people's houses.

104
00:07:21,040 --> 00:07:21,920
I brought him here before.

105
00:07:21,920 --> 00:07:22,399
Lu Zhiyong.

106
00:07:22,759 --> 00:07:23,560
Kill him.

107
00:07:23,560 --> 00:07:24,399
Kill him now.

108
00:07:24,439 --> 00:07:25,199
Now.

109
00:07:25,199 --> 00:07:27,519
Which Xiao Lu are you talking about?

110
00:07:27,759 --> 00:07:28,480
Look.

111
00:07:28,959 --> 00:07:29,600
What is it?

112
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:31,040
He and I are playing on a trampoline.

113
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:33,480
We also took a

114
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:35,199
paralyzed grandpa out.

115
00:07:36,399 --> 00:07:38,519
Here's Xiao Lu and me picking a lock.

116
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:39,600
Picking a lock?

117
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:41,399
You can't go play with Xiao Lu anymore.

118
00:07:41,639 --> 00:07:44,519
Picking locks to play at others' houses is wrong.

119
00:07:44,519 --> 00:07:46,360
Xiao Lu might be in trouble recently.

120
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:47,399
Don't see him again.

121
00:07:47,399 --> 00:07:48,319
What happened?

122
00:07:48,319 --> 00:07:49,600
Don't ask Grandpa why.

123
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:51,399
Don't draw these things anymore.

124
00:07:51,399 --> 00:07:53,439
It's bad if others see or take them.

125
00:07:53,439 --> 00:07:54,839
It's bad evidence.

126
00:07:55,439 --> 00:07:57,360
Let Grandpa destroy them, okay?

127
00:07:57,959 --> 00:07:58,920
Awu, listen to me.

128
00:07:58,920 --> 00:07:59,839
You can't go out anymore.

129
00:07:59,839 --> 00:08:00,879
Awu! Awu!

130
00:08:00,879 --> 00:08:01,439
Awu!

131
00:08:01,439 --> 00:08:02,160
Stop right there.

132
00:08:02,199 --> 00:08:03,319
Awu, stay right there.

133
00:08:03,839 --> 00:08:04,560
Awu, don't you dare!

134
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:06,079
If I can't see Xiao Lu, I'll leave!

135
00:08:06,680 --> 00:08:07,759
Awu, where are you going?

136
00:08:07,759 --> 00:08:08,600
Where are you going?

137
00:08:08,759 --> 00:08:09,360
I want to go home.

138
00:08:09,360 --> 00:08:10,639
This is your home!

139
00:08:10,639 --> 00:08:11,759
I want to go home. I want to go back to the mountain.

140
00:08:11,920 --> 00:08:12,600
I want to find my dad.

141
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:14,199
You're not even my family!

142
00:08:14,199 --> 00:08:15,759
I can play with whoever I want!

143
00:08:15,759 --> 00:08:17,240
Let me tell you, I am your grandfather!

144
00:08:17,240 --> 00:08:18,240
This is your home!

145
00:08:18,240 --> 00:08:19,240
I am your only family!

146
00:08:19,240 --> 00:08:20,839
Do you know that? Do you?

147
00:08:20,839 --> 00:08:21,639
You're lying!

148
00:08:22,120 --> 00:08:22,720
I don't believe you.

149
00:08:24,240 --> 00:08:25,600
You're lying! I don't believe it!

150
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:26,759
Are you crazy, Awu?

151
00:08:26,959 --> 00:08:27,480
Awu!

152
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:28,519
Awu, stop!

153
00:08:29,079 --> 00:08:29,720
If you keep this up...

154
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:31,720
Listen to me, this is your home.

155
00:08:32,840 --> 00:08:34,399
That room was your father's.

156
00:08:34,399 --> 00:08:35,720
Your father's name was Yu Xiaoyue.

157
00:08:35,759 --> 00:08:36,600
He was my son.

158
00:08:37,759 --> 00:08:38,879
It's because your father

159
00:08:38,879 --> 00:08:40,159
did terrible things to your mom and had you.

160
00:08:40,159 --> 00:08:40,960
Do you understand?

161
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:42,600
Stop acting like this! Stop it!

162
00:08:45,679 --> 00:08:46,759
I don't want to live here!

163
00:08:47,279 --> 00:08:49,240
I want to find Ding Ning! I want to find Zhao Yijie!

164
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:51,159
I want to live at Zhao Yijie's place!

165
00:08:51,159 --> 00:08:52,039
Let me tell you,

166
00:08:52,799 --> 00:08:53,879
don't mention Zhao Yijie!

167
00:08:54,279 --> 00:08:55,000
For your sake,

168
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,799
I've done so many terrible things for Zhao Yijie.

169
00:08:56,799 --> 00:08:57,559
Do you know that?

170
00:08:58,679 --> 00:08:59,720
Don't mention that man!

171
00:08:59,720 --> 00:09:00,919
We can't keep these drawings.

172
00:09:00,919 --> 00:09:02,399
They're evidence of the bad things you did.

173
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:04,559
Why are you tearing my drawings?

174
00:09:04,840 --> 00:09:06,000
Don't tear my drawings!

175
00:09:06,120 --> 00:09:06,639
What are you doing?!

176
00:09:09,759 --> 00:09:10,399
Awu!

177
00:09:12,759 --> 00:09:13,480
Awu!

178
00:09:14,519 --> 00:09:15,519
Why are you doing this?!

179
00:09:24,799 --> 00:09:25,919
I didn't mean to.

180
00:09:26,720 --> 00:09:29,360
He suddenly got mad and tore up my drawing.

181
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:31,679
You did it on purpose.

182
00:09:32,039 --> 00:09:33,519
I can't reach your dad right now.

183
00:09:33,840 --> 00:09:34,919
But this is a very serious matter.

184
00:09:34,919 --> 00:09:35,639
You know?

185
00:09:38,279 --> 00:09:39,080
When I was little,

186
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:40,759
before my aunt hit me,

187
00:09:40,919 --> 00:09:42,360
she had the same look on her face as Grandpa Yu.

188
00:09:43,080 --> 00:09:44,399
Dad told me I should fight back.

189
00:09:48,440 --> 00:09:49,720
What exactly is going on?

190
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:52,919
Actually, ever since his fever,

191
00:09:53,159 --> 00:09:55,039
Grandpa Yu couldn't read numbers anymore.

192
00:09:55,919 --> 00:09:57,679
His cooking always tastes like pickles too,

193
00:09:58,720 --> 00:10:00,399
because he adds salt over and over again.

194
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:02,360
He's getting more and more forgetful.

195
00:10:04,039 --> 00:10:05,840
He also suddenly gets angry and throws things.

196
00:10:06,159 --> 00:10:07,840
Then he pretends nothing happened when he sees me.

197
00:10:10,799 --> 00:10:11,600
And then?

198
00:10:21,440 --> 00:10:22,240
And then what?

199
00:10:24,519 --> 00:10:26,039
Zhao Yijie told me to keep an eye on him.

200
00:10:26,480 --> 00:10:28,799
He said if it gets worse, I should call him.

201
00:10:29,960 --> 00:10:31,039
And he'd take him away.

202
00:10:33,559 --> 00:10:34,480
Take him away?

203
00:10:35,120 --> 00:10:36,399
What do you mean, take him away?

204
00:10:37,600 --> 00:10:38,399
I don't know.

205
00:10:38,399 --> 00:10:40,679
He said Grandpa Yu can't look after me anymore.

206
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:44,559
Said he'd take him somewhere that could help him.

207
00:10:46,080 --> 00:10:47,200
But I don't want him to leave.

208
00:10:48,679 --> 00:10:49,840
Even if he can't take care of me,

209
00:10:50,879 --> 00:10:51,799
I can take care of him.

210
00:10:57,960 --> 00:11:00,039
So you didn't want Grandpa's condition to get worse.

211
00:11:00,639 --> 00:11:03,960
You just wanted him to stay with you, right?

212
00:11:09,039 --> 00:11:12,600
Did he actually hit you today?

213
00:11:15,799 --> 00:11:16,840
What do you mean?

214
00:11:17,440 --> 00:11:18,440
It was scarier than that.

215
00:11:24,480 --> 00:11:25,320
What happened to him?

216
00:11:26,519 --> 00:11:27,440
He said...

217
00:11:31,639 --> 00:11:32,440
What did he say?

218
00:11:33,399 --> 00:11:34,159
He said...

219
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:40,320
He said his son is my dad.

220
00:11:41,799 --> 00:11:42,840
My biological dad.

221
00:11:54,559 --> 00:11:56,240
He's just talking nonsense.

222
00:11:56,519 --> 00:11:58,440
You see, he even added salt twice.

223
00:11:58,480 --> 00:12:00,120
So he definitely took his meds twice.

224
00:12:00,120 --> 00:12:01,720
Too much medication makes you confused.

225
00:12:01,879 --> 00:12:02,759
And once you're confused,

226
00:12:02,799 --> 00:12:05,559
you mix up hope and reality.

227
00:12:05,559 --> 00:12:06,279
Right?

228
00:12:06,440 --> 00:12:07,559
Just talking nonsense.

229
00:12:09,200 --> 00:12:10,000
Are you the family?

230
00:12:11,559 --> 00:12:12,360
Yes, what's wrong?

231
00:12:12,960 --> 00:12:14,679
He refuses anesthesia for his stitches.

232
00:12:14,799 --> 00:12:16,399
But with his heart rate and blood pressure...

233
00:12:16,559 --> 00:12:18,080
you family members should try persuading him.

234
00:12:19,039 --> 00:12:20,799
Are you sure you don't want anesthesia?

235
00:12:23,240 --> 00:12:24,120
We're sure.

236
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:27,919
What do you think could be

237
00:12:28,120 --> 00:12:30,000
more painful than that stab from Awu?

238
00:12:41,480 --> 00:12:42,720
Okay, come on.

239
00:12:43,279 --> 00:12:44,120
I'll go get ready then.

240
00:12:58,480 --> 00:13:00,799
I won't ask, so don't pretend.

241
00:13:08,120 --> 00:13:11,080
Actually, I find it pretty ridiculous.

242
00:13:12,799 --> 00:13:14,519
For the adoption paperwork,

243
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:19,320
I even considered a fake marriage with Shasha.

244
00:13:20,240 --> 00:13:23,000
But at this age...

245
00:13:23,320 --> 00:13:24,440
Alright, say no more.

246
00:13:24,559 --> 00:13:25,440
I'll stay with you.

247
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:36,480
I'm so ridiculous.

248
00:14:37,240 --> 00:14:39,039
Just for the adoption papers,

249
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:42,639
I even considered a fake marriage with Shasha.

250
00:15:05,679 --> 00:15:06,639
Where did you go with Grandpa?

251
00:15:06,639 --> 00:15:08,159
Why didn't you tell me?

252
00:15:08,159 --> 00:15:09,919
We just went on a trip for a few days.

253
00:15:10,039 --> 00:15:12,279
You could've at least texted me about the trip.

254
00:15:12,279 --> 00:15:13,480
You didn't even answer your phone.

255
00:15:13,559 --> 00:15:15,159
We just wanted some peace and quiet for a few days.

256
00:15:15,159 --> 00:15:16,240
Sorry about that.

257
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:23,519
He said

258
00:15:24,159 --> 00:15:28,080
He said his son is my dad.

259
00:15:29,639 --> 00:15:30,639
My biological dad.

260
00:15:36,159 --> 00:15:37,879
Even though I've never met Mr. Yu's son,

261
00:15:38,039 --> 00:15:40,600
I heard he was just like our Awu.

262
00:15:40,720 --> 00:15:42,120
Smart and bright.

263
00:15:42,639 --> 00:15:44,919
He also liked math a lot, right?

264
00:15:45,279 --> 00:15:46,000
Good at sports, too.

265
00:15:46,919 --> 00:15:48,000
He played basketball really well.

266
00:15:48,399 --> 00:15:50,039
I signed the letter of forgiveness.

267
00:15:51,480 --> 00:15:52,840
I didn't attend the second trial.

268
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,039
I had never even met you back then.

269
00:15:55,360 --> 00:15:57,639
You sure know a lot about my family.

270
00:16:04,320 --> 00:16:07,399
Hello, the number you dialed is powered off.

271
00:16:13,639 --> 00:16:14,960
About Yu Songfan,

272
00:16:15,879 --> 00:16:17,000
Do you know anything?

273
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:26,519
Hello?

274
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:28,919
Look someone up for me.

275
00:16:51,399 --> 00:16:52,039
Hello?

276
00:16:52,519 --> 00:16:53,600
It's Xu Ruqing.

277
00:16:54,279 --> 00:16:55,679
Is Zhao Yijie with you?

278
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:57,759
No, he's not.

279
00:16:58,279 --> 00:17:00,720
Then since the New Year,

280
00:17:01,320 --> 00:17:02,759
have you two seen each other?

281
00:17:03,240 --> 00:17:05,519
Just on New Year's Eve.

282
00:17:05,599 --> 00:17:06,799
Haven't seen him since.

283
00:17:07,039 --> 00:17:07,759
Is something wrong?

284
00:17:07,880 --> 00:17:08,720
New Year's Eve?

285
00:17:09,759 --> 00:17:10,400
Yeah.

286
00:17:11,920 --> 00:17:14,480
Ding Ning, Awu, and I went to his place for dinner.

287
00:17:14,640 --> 00:17:16,599
But he said something came up, so we left.

288
00:17:17,680 --> 00:17:19,079
Why are you looking for him?

289
00:17:21,519 --> 00:17:22,559
Well, please,

290
00:17:22,960 --> 00:17:24,559
if he contacts you,

291
00:17:24,880 --> 00:17:26,160
let me know right away.

292
00:17:26,839 --> 00:17:27,519
Thanks.

293
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:28,680
Will do.

294
00:17:41,960 --> 00:17:42,519
Hello?

295
00:17:42,799 --> 00:17:43,839
Is this Mr. Yu Songfan?

296
00:17:44,119 --> 00:17:45,400
This is Panda Safes.

297
00:17:45,759 --> 00:17:46,759
We're calling to let you know

298
00:17:47,039 --> 00:17:48,839
that if you take photos and leave a review,

299
00:17:48,839 --> 00:17:49,680
you'll get fifty yuan cashback.

300
00:17:49,960 --> 00:17:51,200
Would you be interested in participating?

301
00:17:52,119 --> 00:17:53,920
I was just about to call you.

302
00:17:53,920 --> 00:17:56,359
Did I... Did I order a safe?

303
00:17:56,359 --> 00:17:57,319
When did I order it?

304
00:17:57,319 --> 00:17:58,440
Our delivery records show

305
00:17:58,440 --> 00:17:59,759
you placed the order on New Year's Day,

306
00:17:59,839 --> 00:18:00,839
and received it on the fourth.

307
00:18:01,079 --> 00:18:02,519
That's not right, sir.

308
00:18:03,519 --> 00:18:05,680
Today is the third day of the new year.

309
00:18:05,680 --> 00:18:06,759
It's only the third.

310
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:08,200
You must be mistaken.

311
00:18:08,200 --> 00:18:10,640
Sir, today is already the fifth.

312
00:18:10,759 --> 00:18:11,640
Wait a minute.

313
00:18:15,519 --> 00:18:16,799
Right. I'm sorry.

314
00:18:17,119 --> 00:18:18,799
We've sent you a text message.

315
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:21,079
You can reply to it to leave a review.

316
00:18:22,559 --> 00:18:22,960
Okay.

317
00:18:22,960 --> 00:18:26,000
I'll... I'll reply to your text later.

318
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:27,000
Sorry about that. Thank you.

319
00:18:31,400 --> 00:18:33,079
Why did I order this thing?

320
00:18:44,480 --> 00:18:46,519
Has Mr. Zhao contacted you recently?

321
00:18:48,559 --> 00:18:50,359
When was the last time he contacted you?

322
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:51,640
Including privately.

323
00:18:53,599 --> 00:18:54,640
Did something happen?

324
00:18:59,440 --> 00:19:01,759
His last contact wasn't actually with me.

325
00:19:02,119 --> 00:19:04,279
It was at Zhao Yijie's house on New Year's.

326
00:19:04,279 --> 00:19:05,599
He made a phone call back.

327
00:19:07,440 --> 00:19:08,599
And after that? Nothing.

328
00:19:10,079 --> 00:19:11,920
I've been texting him these past few days, but no reply.

329
00:19:14,880 --> 00:19:16,039
That's weird.

330
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:18,799
He's never been like this before.

331
00:19:23,440 --> 00:19:24,400
He's unreachable.

332
00:19:25,720 --> 00:19:28,039
Ding Ning, you must keep this a secret.

333
00:19:28,920 --> 00:19:30,960
Think carefully and try to remember.

334
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:32,839
When was the exact last time he contacted you?

335
00:19:32,839 --> 00:19:34,400
Did he give you any tasks?

336
00:19:34,400 --> 00:19:35,319
Even hinted ones count.

337
00:19:35,319 --> 00:19:36,960
You know how he likes to beat around the bush.

338
00:19:37,160 --> 00:19:37,799
No.

339
00:19:38,720 --> 00:19:39,759
Besides him,

340
00:19:40,119 --> 00:19:41,240
I can't reach Liang Zidong either.

341
00:19:41,240 --> 00:19:42,279
Liang Zidong isn't important.

342
00:19:42,279 --> 00:19:43,680
We're talking about him right now.

343
00:19:46,599 --> 00:19:48,160
Are you sure you two aren't plotting something,

344
00:19:48,160 --> 00:19:49,400
or setting up some kind of trap?

345
00:19:49,720 --> 00:19:51,960
Zhao Yijie has never done this before.

346
00:19:52,240 --> 00:19:54,119
I've asked around at his usual spots,

347
00:19:54,119 --> 00:19:55,559
and there's no record of him going abroad.

348
00:19:55,559 --> 00:19:57,079
Don't you think this is strange?

349
00:20:00,799 --> 00:20:02,400
Did you find out anything these past two days?

350
00:20:07,240 --> 00:20:09,319
I did actually go over the timeline.

351
00:20:11,519 --> 00:20:13,880
After that fake litigation base incident,

352
00:20:14,279 --> 00:20:16,519
he recommended you to the higher-ups

353
00:20:16,519 --> 00:20:17,839
to be his successor.

354
00:20:18,599 --> 00:20:19,440
And then,

355
00:20:20,440 --> 00:20:21,640
after the New Year,

356
00:20:22,519 --> 00:20:23,920
no one has been able to reach him.

357
00:20:32,559 --> 00:20:33,279
Prosecutor Lei.

358
00:20:34,720 --> 00:20:36,119
Prosecutor Lei, I can't reach Director Ma.

359
00:20:36,279 --> 00:20:37,599
Did something happen to her?

360
00:20:42,240 --> 00:20:44,839
Her family of three got into a car crash over the holidays.

361
00:20:46,759 --> 00:20:47,720
A car crash?

362
00:20:50,960 --> 00:20:52,319
Prosecutor Ma's husband was severely injured.

363
00:20:52,759 --> 00:20:54,960
She was also injured and is currently recovering.

364
00:20:59,079 --> 00:20:59,880
That's not right.

365
00:21:01,079 --> 00:21:02,240
Something's not right about this.

366
00:21:04,440 --> 00:21:05,920
After the Fuxia Group incident,

367
00:21:06,039 --> 00:21:06,880
Liang Zidong lost contact.

368
00:21:06,880 --> 00:21:07,880
Zhao Yijie went missing.

369
00:21:07,960 --> 00:21:09,680
And now this has happened to Director Ma.

370
00:21:10,400 --> 00:21:11,839
There has to be a connection here.

371
00:21:11,960 --> 00:21:13,839
Right now, even the fate of the investigation team

372
00:21:13,839 --> 00:21:14,799
is uncertain.

373
00:21:16,839 --> 00:21:17,400
Is...

374
00:21:19,079 --> 00:21:20,279
is everyone being disbanded?

375
00:21:20,279 --> 00:21:20,960
Or...

376
00:21:21,480 --> 00:21:22,920
I've already told you enough.

377
00:21:23,440 --> 00:21:25,759
As for the rest, you understand.

378
00:21:29,279 --> 00:21:29,960
Prosecutor Lei.

379
00:21:30,039 --> 00:21:32,880
Can I go visit Director Ma?

380
00:22:06,960 --> 00:22:08,279
Where do you guys want to go for winter break?

381
00:22:08,279 --> 00:22:09,359
I want to go to the water park.

382
00:22:09,759 --> 00:22:10,759
I want hot pot.

383
00:22:10,920 --> 00:22:12,200
Let's go bungee jumping, okay?

384
00:22:12,200 --> 00:22:13,680
I want to eat, not jump.

385
00:22:13,880 --> 00:22:14,960
I want hot pot.

386
00:22:14,960 --> 00:22:15,599
Let's go to karaoke.

387
00:22:15,599 --> 00:22:16,279
I want to go to the water park.

388
00:22:46,920 --> 00:22:47,799
Isn't that what's-his-face?

389
00:22:48,079 --> 00:22:49,160
The kid who dropped by.

390
00:22:49,480 --> 00:22:50,680
He even got a haircut.

391
00:22:50,839 --> 00:22:51,839
Looks pretty sharp, actually.

392
00:22:52,799 --> 00:22:53,759
I want to turn myself in.

393
00:22:54,119 --> 00:22:55,359
Whose place did you drop by this time?

394
00:22:56,519 --> 00:22:57,319
I killed someone.

395
00:23:15,599 --> 00:23:16,599
Expand the search area.

396
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:26,640
Sun.

397
00:23:26,880 --> 00:23:27,720
What do you mean?

398
00:23:27,880 --> 00:23:28,799
You said on the phone

399
00:23:28,799 --> 00:23:30,839
that the kid who stole turned himself in for murder.

400
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:31,839
What are you talking about?

401
00:23:31,839 --> 00:23:32,920
You remember Lu Zhiyong, right?

402
00:23:32,920 --> 00:23:33,799
The kid who brought the paralyzed old man

403
00:23:33,799 --> 00:23:35,480
to the entrance of our station.

404
00:23:35,680 --> 00:23:36,480
I know.

405
00:23:36,559 --> 00:23:38,599
Wait, he didn't steal anything.

406
00:23:38,920 --> 00:23:40,799
He just picked a lock and went into someone's house to play.

407
00:23:40,799 --> 00:23:42,000
Not only did he not steal anything,

408
00:23:42,119 --> 00:23:43,400
he even helped them clean up.

409
00:23:43,799 --> 00:23:45,319
So, what happened to the little guy?

410
00:23:45,920 --> 00:23:47,400
He came to the station this afternoon.

411
00:23:47,440 --> 00:23:49,559
He said he killed someone.

412
00:23:51,079 --> 00:23:53,200
Wait, what nonsense is he spouting?

413
00:23:53,240 --> 00:23:54,640
Is he out of his mind?

414
00:23:54,759 --> 00:23:55,799
At first,

415
00:23:55,799 --> 00:23:57,079
we had the exact same reaction as you.

416
00:23:57,279 --> 00:23:59,079
We didn't even let him into the interrogation room.

417
00:23:59,319 --> 00:24:00,480
We just gave him a lecture,

418
00:24:00,480 --> 00:24:01,279
telling him

419
00:24:01,279 --> 00:24:03,559
that making a false police report carries serious consequences.

420
00:24:03,640 --> 00:24:04,400
As it turned out,

421
00:24:04,400 --> 00:24:05,880
the kid was really stubborn.

422
00:24:05,880 --> 00:24:07,119
He kept running his mouth.

423
00:24:07,279 --> 00:24:08,079
The more he talked,

424
00:24:08,079 --> 00:24:09,519
the more Wang and the others felt

425
00:24:09,880 --> 00:24:10,960
they should just follow protocol.

426
00:24:11,119 --> 00:24:12,960
A coward like him? Murder?

427
00:24:13,599 --> 00:24:14,480
Did you contact his parents?

428
00:24:14,480 --> 00:24:15,119
Where is his mom?

429
00:24:15,119 --> 00:24:16,799
That's what we thought earlier.

430
00:24:17,640 --> 00:24:19,039
According to protocol,

431
00:24:19,160 --> 00:24:20,880
since the little guy is under eighteen,

432
00:24:20,920 --> 00:24:22,279
we have to find his guardian.

433
00:24:22,880 --> 00:24:24,759
So we went to his house to find his mom.

434
00:24:24,759 --> 00:24:26,200
As soon as we went in, guess what?

435
00:24:26,400 --> 00:24:27,160
What happened?

436
00:24:27,160 --> 00:24:27,920
Nobody move!

437
00:24:27,960 --> 00:24:29,160
Put down what's in your hands!

438
00:24:29,400 --> 00:24:30,000
Put it down!

439
00:24:30,000 --> 00:24:31,000
What are you doing?

440
00:24:31,039 --> 00:24:32,799
The lady was washing clothes.

441
00:24:32,880 --> 00:24:34,079
The clothes were covered in blood.

442
00:24:36,240 --> 00:24:37,839
While we were at it, we found the shoes,

443
00:24:37,839 --> 00:24:39,200
and even the murder weapon.

444
00:24:39,440 --> 00:24:40,400
All of it was in their house.

445
00:24:41,400 --> 00:24:42,200
There were bloodstains.

446
00:24:43,079 --> 00:24:44,079
As soon as we asked the lady,

447
00:24:44,079 --> 00:24:45,920
it was only then she realized the kid had killed someone.

448
00:24:45,920 --> 00:24:46,759
By the looks of it,

449
00:24:46,759 --> 00:24:47,960
she seemed even more confused than us.

450
00:24:48,920 --> 00:24:49,759
Wait.

451
00:24:50,319 --> 00:24:52,400
What murder weapon? How bad is it?

452
00:24:52,440 --> 00:24:53,799
Can I take a look at the evidence photos?

453
00:24:54,440 --> 00:24:56,400
The weirdest part is yet to come.

454
00:24:57,119 --> 00:24:58,440
When we actually had him take us

455
00:24:58,440 --> 00:25:00,240
to where he killed and buried the body...

456
00:25:03,559 --> 00:25:04,240
What happened?

457
00:25:05,519 --> 00:25:06,240
Nothing.

458
00:25:06,599 --> 00:25:07,759
The body wasn't there.

459
00:25:09,480 --> 00:25:10,440
I'll ask you one more time.

460
00:25:10,720 --> 00:25:12,039
Are you sure the body is here?

461
00:25:12,720 --> 00:25:13,519
I killed someone,

462
00:25:13,519 --> 00:25:14,720
and the body is buried right here.

463
00:25:16,039 --> 00:25:17,880
I don't know how it disappeared.

464
00:25:18,640 --> 00:25:20,480
We couldn't find the body at all.

465
00:25:21,680 --> 00:25:22,960
You couldn't find the body?

466
00:25:23,039 --> 00:25:23,759
Right.

467
00:25:24,400 --> 00:25:26,039
Even as we're talking right now,

468
00:25:26,039 --> 00:25:27,720
Wang and the others are tearing the place apart

469
00:25:27,720 --> 00:25:29,200
looking for the guy who got stabbed to death.

470
00:25:29,880 --> 00:25:31,240
What about the surveillance footage nearby?

471
00:25:31,559 --> 00:25:32,680
Did you submit a request for it?

472
00:25:32,680 --> 00:25:34,519
Yes, it's being processed.

473
00:25:35,279 --> 00:25:36,720
And those clothes we found

474
00:25:36,920 --> 00:25:39,200
have already been sent to your forensics unit.

475
00:25:39,319 --> 00:25:40,400
Just wait for the results.

476
00:25:43,759 --> 00:25:44,720
How could this be?

477
00:25:44,720 --> 00:25:45,720
Here's what I think.

478
00:25:46,440 --> 00:25:48,400
Whether the kid committed a crime or not,

479
00:25:48,759 --> 00:25:50,359
we have our procedures,

480
00:25:50,359 --> 00:25:51,640
we have our regulations,

481
00:25:51,759 --> 00:25:53,680
and we have to investigate according to the law.

482
00:25:54,759 --> 00:25:56,519
Which interrogation room is he in now?

483
00:25:58,359 --> 00:25:59,079
What are you thinking?

484
00:25:59,519 --> 00:26:01,000
You can't question him right now.

485
00:26:02,319 --> 00:26:03,680
I won't question him.

486
00:26:04,160 --> 00:26:05,319
I'm bringing him some food.

487
00:26:12,400 --> 00:26:13,200
Uncle Fan.

488
00:26:14,160 --> 00:26:15,720
I'm not in charge of your case.

489
00:26:16,559 --> 00:26:17,799
I just ordered some takeout.

490
00:26:17,799 --> 00:26:18,640
I knew you were here,

491
00:26:18,799 --> 00:26:19,920
so I brought some over for you to eat.

492
00:26:27,920 --> 00:26:28,960
You got your bangs cut.

493
00:26:29,519 --> 00:26:30,720
Looks terrible.

494
00:26:32,599 --> 00:26:34,839
None of your business. Leave.

495
00:26:38,720 --> 00:26:40,759
It's 3 a.m. Aren't you hungry?

496
00:26:41,119 --> 00:26:42,000
Quick, take a bite.

497
00:26:42,119 --> 00:26:43,000
I'll leave after you eat.

498
00:26:45,119 --> 00:26:46,839
Come on, Xiaoyong, eat.

499
00:26:56,920 --> 00:26:57,720
Thank you.

500
00:26:58,440 --> 00:26:59,200
You're welcome.

501
00:27:01,400 --> 00:27:02,680
Slow down, slow down.

502
00:27:02,880 --> 00:27:03,920
Don't choke.

503
00:27:11,680 --> 00:27:13,160
My mentor once told me

504
00:27:13,720 --> 00:27:15,000
that by looking at how someone eats,

505
00:27:15,440 --> 00:27:16,920
you can tell if they're a bad person.

506
00:27:19,359 --> 00:27:20,599
Someone who enjoys their food this much

507
00:27:21,920 --> 00:27:23,240
isn't capable of doing terrible things.

508
00:27:28,599 --> 00:27:31,440
I went to your house on New Year's Eve.

509
00:27:34,880 --> 00:27:36,319
You and your mom weren't home,

510
00:27:37,119 --> 00:27:38,400
but the food was still warm.

511
00:27:38,640 --> 00:27:40,519
I remember the exact time clearly.

512
00:27:43,079 --> 00:27:44,240
Did you have time to commit the crime?

513
00:27:51,119 --> 00:27:52,319
I didn't tell anyone.

514
00:27:52,720 --> 00:27:53,680
Because if I did,

515
00:27:53,960 --> 00:27:55,319
I might lose the right to help you.

516
00:28:04,160 --> 00:28:06,240
Uncle Fan...

517
00:28:09,400 --> 00:28:11,319
Xiaoyong, have some water.

518
00:28:33,079 --> 00:28:34,200
The truth will come out.

519
00:29:00,680 --> 00:29:01,599
Which tube are we on?

520
00:29:02,200 --> 00:29:03,240
This should be the third.

521
00:29:16,319 --> 00:29:17,119
Mr. Xu.

522
00:29:17,559 --> 00:29:18,799
How are things with Liang Zidong?

523
00:29:21,200 --> 00:29:22,079
We're working on it.

524
00:29:24,720 --> 00:29:27,279
You need to keep a close eye on Xiaolu's situation.

525
00:29:27,920 --> 00:29:31,240
His mother has been acting up lately.

526
00:29:33,079 --> 00:29:34,319
Things have been really chaotic lately.

527
00:29:36,640 --> 00:29:37,960
Does it really have to come to this?

528
00:29:41,359 --> 00:29:42,319
Okay, I got it.

529
00:29:52,960 --> 00:29:53,680
One more shot.

530
00:30:11,519 --> 00:30:12,559
Scan successful.

531
00:30:16,720 --> 00:30:18,119
Didn't I tell you?

532
00:30:18,119 --> 00:30:20,440
Don't contact me again after the surrender.

533
00:30:20,440 --> 00:30:21,240
It's dangerous.

534
00:30:21,799 --> 00:30:23,039
I was very careful.

535
00:30:23,279 --> 00:30:24,480
I told the police

536
00:30:24,759 --> 00:30:26,319
I came back for a change of clothes.

537
00:30:26,759 --> 00:30:27,640
What is it?

538
00:30:28,759 --> 00:30:30,200
Why is the body missing?

539
00:30:30,200 --> 00:30:31,400
That wasn't part of the plan.

540
00:30:31,400 --> 00:30:32,640
That's not your concern.

541
00:30:33,960 --> 00:30:35,079
What's the situation on your end?

542
00:30:36,799 --> 00:30:38,079
The police took my statement.

543
00:30:39,160 --> 00:30:40,200
The clothes and shoes,

544
00:30:40,599 --> 00:30:41,559
just as you said,

545
00:30:41,559 --> 00:30:42,640
I washed some of them,

546
00:30:42,759 --> 00:30:44,599
and then they took them away.

547
00:30:48,319 --> 00:30:49,039
Good.

548
00:30:50,720 --> 00:30:52,119
You won't be doing this for nothing.

549
00:30:54,599 --> 00:30:56,759
Don't deposit this money in the bank.

550
00:30:56,759 --> 00:30:57,920
And don't keep it at home either.

551
00:30:58,160 --> 00:30:59,000
From now on,

552
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:00,240
start borrowing money from everywhere.

553
00:31:00,759 --> 00:31:02,599
Keep all the chat records.

554
00:31:03,279 --> 00:31:04,480
In case anyone traces the money,

555
00:31:04,480 --> 00:31:05,599
you'll have a reasonable explanation.

556
00:31:06,920 --> 00:31:07,680
Okay.

557
00:31:08,680 --> 00:31:10,599
B-But the body is missing.

558
00:31:10,720 --> 00:31:12,400
They're wearing Xiaoyong down every day,

559
00:31:12,599 --> 00:31:13,440
and still won't file the case.

560
00:31:13,440 --> 00:31:14,839
There's been a slight complication.

561
00:31:16,759 --> 00:31:17,880
Just remember,

562
00:31:18,200 --> 00:31:19,559
make sure the kid sticks to his story.

563
00:31:20,680 --> 00:31:21,519
Are we clear?

564
00:31:23,559 --> 00:31:24,319
Okay.

565
00:31:24,319 --> 00:31:25,440
All right, let's leave it at that.

566
00:31:26,880 --> 00:31:27,599
Um...

567
00:31:28,240 --> 00:31:29,119
Brother Kong...

568
00:31:30,000 --> 00:31:32,920
A police officer came to my house on New Year's Day.

569
00:31:32,920 --> 00:31:34,720
I've been so distracted these past few days

570
00:31:35,000 --> 00:31:36,039
that I didn't even notice.

571
00:31:39,440 --> 00:31:42,079
Where are they? The New Year's gifts.

572
00:31:50,920 --> 00:31:52,480
He left some New Year's gifts for us.

573
00:31:52,480 --> 00:31:53,759
On New Year's Eve?

574
00:31:54,039 --> 00:31:54,880
What time?

575
00:31:55,079 --> 00:31:58,200
That officer said the food was still hot.

576
00:32:00,359 --> 00:32:01,119
This means

577
00:32:01,759 --> 00:32:04,279
the timeline you gave Xiaoyong

578
00:32:04,279 --> 00:32:05,160
won't add up anymore, right?

579
00:32:06,200 --> 00:32:07,480
Do you know his name?

580
00:32:08,240 --> 00:32:09,000
Fan Dong.

581
00:32:10,359 --> 00:32:11,119
Okay.

582
00:32:12,519 --> 00:32:13,240
Got it.

583
00:32:14,640 --> 00:32:15,720
No, wait...

584
00:32:16,480 --> 00:32:18,079
If we get exposed

585
00:32:18,640 --> 00:32:19,480
and he breaks,

586
00:32:19,759 --> 00:32:21,160
what will happen to our Xiaoyong?

587
00:32:22,680 --> 00:32:23,480
Don't forget,

588
00:32:24,200 --> 00:32:26,119
Lu Zhiyong really did kill someone.

589
00:32:49,000 --> 00:32:51,279
Awu, you only have two assignments today.

590
00:32:51,279 --> 00:32:52,920
Just Chinese and math.

591
00:32:53,200 --> 00:32:53,880
Really?

592
00:32:54,440 --> 00:32:55,319
Listen to me.

593
00:32:55,319 --> 00:32:58,160
Grandpa is going to the hospital for a checkup today.

594
00:32:58,359 --> 00:32:59,319
Sister Ding Ning

595
00:32:59,319 --> 00:33:00,559
will come take you to school.

596
00:33:00,680 --> 00:33:01,440
Grandpa.

597
00:33:01,440 --> 00:33:02,640
Are you feeling okay?

598
00:33:04,039 --> 00:33:05,960
I'm fine. Grandpa is perfectly healthy.

599
00:33:07,519 --> 00:33:08,880
Drink your milk.

600
00:33:09,200 --> 00:33:10,039
She's here.

601
00:33:14,440 --> 00:33:15,079
I'm here.

602
00:33:18,880 --> 00:33:19,759
Are you okay?

603
00:33:20,079 --> 00:33:21,519
You look terrible today.

604
00:33:21,519 --> 00:33:22,319
Are you not feeling well?

605
00:33:24,759 --> 00:33:25,799
Liang Zidong is dead.

606
00:33:27,079 --> 00:33:28,240
How could it be so sudden?

607
00:33:31,559 --> 00:33:32,400
Have some water.

608
00:33:34,359 --> 00:33:34,960
His wife said

609
00:33:34,960 --> 00:33:37,039
he injected himself with an overdose of insulin.

610
00:33:37,279 --> 00:33:38,039
When he was found,

611
00:33:38,039 --> 00:33:39,680
he had already died from severe hypoglycemia.

612
00:33:41,200 --> 00:33:42,559
I really need to ask around.

613
00:33:47,480 --> 00:33:48,880
Any news from Zhao Yijie?

614
00:33:49,039 --> 00:33:49,839
No.

615
00:33:50,079 --> 00:33:51,000
Haven't seen him in a while.

616
00:33:57,279 --> 00:33:59,240
A lot of things have been really strange lately.

617
00:34:01,079 --> 00:34:02,000
Once I'm done with work,

618
00:34:02,319 --> 00:34:03,480
let's have a good talk.

619
00:34:04,799 --> 00:34:05,680
Sure.

620
00:34:07,079 --> 00:34:07,799
Awu.

621
00:34:08,119 --> 00:34:09,519
Let's go. Hurry, we're going to be late.

622
00:34:10,079 --> 00:34:10,760
Hurry!

623
00:34:11,000 --> 00:34:12,400
I'll pick him up after school today.

624
00:34:12,480 --> 00:34:13,199
After my court hearing,

625
00:34:13,199 --> 00:34:14,559
it'll be right around the time he gets out.

626
00:34:14,559 --> 00:34:15,159
We're running late.

627
00:34:15,159 --> 00:34:15,880
Say goodbye to Grandpa.

628
00:34:16,000 --> 00:34:16,639
Bye.

629
00:34:16,760 --> 00:34:17,360
Bye, Grandpa!

630
00:34:17,360 --> 00:34:18,400
Alright, thank you.

631
00:34:41,559 --> 00:34:42,079
Hello?

632
00:34:42,079 --> 00:34:43,079
This is Zhao Yijie.

633
00:34:43,320 --> 00:34:44,800
Where have you been all this time?

634
00:34:44,800 --> 00:34:46,440
I don't have time to explain right now.

635
00:34:46,440 --> 00:34:48,000
There's a van downstairs.

636
00:34:48,000 --> 00:34:49,400
Ending in 311.

637
00:34:49,599 --> 00:34:50,280
Get in first.

638
00:34:50,639 --> 00:34:52,639
I have to go to the hospital for a checkup today.

639
00:34:53,039 --> 00:34:53,760
I don't have time.

640
00:35:10,159 --> 00:35:12,159
I saw 311. Where are you?

641
00:35:12,159 --> 00:35:13,039
Did you get in the car?

642
00:35:17,599 --> 00:35:18,440
Where are you?

643
00:35:19,480 --> 00:35:20,039
Hello?

644
00:35:20,679 --> 00:35:22,440
Is your Alzheimer's acting up again?

645
00:35:23,159 --> 00:35:24,320
Seriously, what are you doing?

646
00:35:24,599 --> 00:35:26,400
Didn't we agree to meet today?

647
00:35:28,800 --> 00:35:29,880
I made plans with you?

648
00:35:30,400 --> 00:35:31,000
What for?

649
00:35:31,280 --> 00:35:32,599
The navigation is already set.

650
00:35:33,079 --> 00:35:33,920
See you at the destination.

651
00:35:42,920 --> 00:35:44,840
Zhao Yijie, what am I going there for?

652
00:35:45,000 --> 00:35:46,880
It's important. Hurry up.

653
00:36:06,719 --> 00:36:08,639
Zhao Yijie, tell me.

654
00:36:09,760 --> 00:36:11,039
What is that in the back?

655
00:36:11,119 --> 00:36:11,920
A freezer.

656
00:36:12,159 --> 00:36:13,360
I know it's a freezer.

657
00:36:13,360 --> 00:36:14,719
What's inside the freezer?

658
00:36:14,719 --> 00:36:16,480
I'll tell you when we reach our destination.

659
00:36:16,480 --> 00:36:18,440
Tell me right now. Speak.

660
00:36:18,679 --> 00:36:20,599
Or I'm driving straight to the police station.

661
00:36:20,599 --> 00:36:21,199
Yu Songfan...

662
00:36:21,199 --> 00:36:23,320
Tell me right now. Speak!

663
00:36:29,320 --> 00:36:30,679
Actually, that night,

664
00:36:32,000 --> 00:36:33,239
the kid was terrified.

665
00:36:37,519 --> 00:36:38,679
While he was taking a shower,

666
00:36:39,360 --> 00:36:41,559
we suddenly noticed scratches on his neck.

667
00:36:42,000 --> 00:36:43,360
Didn't you say...

668
00:36:44,960 --> 00:36:45,719
Right.

669
00:36:46,280 --> 00:36:47,760
He was too nervous back then.

670
00:36:48,199 --> 00:36:50,960
He got scratched while struggling with the victim.

671
00:36:53,679 --> 00:36:54,480
So that means...

672
00:36:54,480 --> 00:36:55,840
no matter how flawlessly

673
00:36:56,000 --> 00:36:59,199
you framed Lu Zhiyong before,

674
00:36:59,480 --> 00:37:02,280
as long as there's tissue left under the victim's nails,

675
00:37:02,440 --> 00:37:04,440
all the medical examiner needs is a simple

676
00:37:04,440 --> 00:37:05,440
DNA extraction,

677
00:37:05,519 --> 00:37:06,519
and they'll find out

678
00:37:07,400 --> 00:37:08,800
that the killer is someone else.

679
00:37:09,599 --> 00:37:10,400
You guys...

680
00:37:11,039 --> 00:37:11,840
Say it.

681
00:37:14,800 --> 00:37:15,559
Keep talking!

682
00:37:16,360 --> 00:37:17,800
Don't tell me what's in the back is...

683
00:37:25,360 --> 00:37:27,760
Old Yu, let me tell you.

684
00:37:28,440 --> 00:37:30,440
The police will never find this body.

685
00:37:30,920 --> 00:37:33,079
So knowing me as you do,

686
00:37:33,800 --> 00:37:35,639
where would the body be right now?

687
00:37:52,480 --> 00:37:53,920
Zhao Yijie, what are you doing?

688
00:37:57,719 --> 00:38:00,039
I want you to dump the body, of course.

689
00:38:04,400 --> 00:38:05,320
Are you crazy?

690
00:38:06,079 --> 00:38:08,239
I won't help you do this.

691
00:38:08,880 --> 00:38:11,239
Fine, then run.

692
00:38:12,039 --> 00:38:14,119
Your fingerprints are all over the steering wheel.

693
00:38:14,440 --> 00:38:15,960
And the cameras at every intersection

694
00:38:15,960 --> 00:38:17,559
have caught you on tape.

695
00:38:18,159 --> 00:38:20,440
Where can you run to now?

696
00:38:27,400 --> 00:38:28,559
So stop wasting time.

697
00:38:28,920 --> 00:38:30,679
Hurry up and finish the job.

698
00:38:31,880 --> 00:38:32,519
Hurry!

699
00:38:36,960 --> 00:38:37,840
You bastard!
